# Signed absolute value in zero-knowledge over Goldilocks. sabs(x) = |x| for a SIGNED x in
# [-2^31, 2^31). Composes the existing signed comparison + if (sabs(x) = if x < 0 then -x else x) —
# no new gadget, no verifier change. The proof reveals only |x|, never x's sign or value.
#   glass prove examples/prove/signed_abs.glass x=-5    # -> result: 5, ACCEPT
sabs(x)
